on it's  going to go  that low so with the math piece out of  the way  let's look at what democrats are doing  so far bearing in mind that we're still  in the pre-primary phase democrats need  to run good campaigns  with progressive ideas that are popular  of course  but democrats also need to at least  somewhat appeal  to red state voters and moderates in  purple states on the issues that clearly  matter right now as i've said before  as a strategy get out the vote is much  more powerful  than arguing with trumpists but  it still makes sense to at least stake  out  positions generally speaking that will  be  reasonable to some fraction of those  moderate republican voters now there's a  necessary disclaimer here  i'm being strategic here i'm not talking  about what i like  and what my politics are i'm talking  about winning 2020.  think about immigration first it's  disgusting  what's happening at the border it's a  real humanitarian crisis  but most of the conversations that  democratic candidates are having  are ridiculous and debate moderators are  hugely to blame for this as i've talked  about before  what's happening with the discussion  around deportations  on the right is an absolute fantasy  right i mean  we're not going to deport 12 million  people who are in the united states  illegally  nor would we want to deport the 12  million people  that are in the united states illegally  if people are committing violent crimes  and they're here illegally okay they're  now you're talking about people that it  makes sense to deport  but the reality is that there are  multiple industries that depend on these  undocumented immigrants including  agriculture  including the restaurant industry and  they're a hugely positive influence on  our society both economically and  culturally  from any number of standpoints  from an american dream standpoint from a  work ethic standpoint in basically every  way that we can imagine  almost all of these undocumented  immigrants are 