e been saying  is not going to convince a lifelong  midwestern republican  to vote for a democrat and i've said  this before  when we hear about all of these trump  voters in the midwest who are  angry with trump or disapprove of trump  or our farmers and recognize that trump  is ruining their businesses  that doesn't mean that you're going to  go out and vote for a democrat in  november of 2020. lifelong republicans  who don't approve of trump aren't  necessarily voting  for joe biden or bernie sanders or  elizabeth warren  so something more needs to be done there  and it generally relates to the economic  anxieties of middle america  that hillary clinton didn't do a good  job of addressing in an appropriate  enough way  this is just the reality i'm not saying  the narrative about disadvantaged white  people  is based in any reality it's ridiculous  what i am  saying is that without addressing some  of these issues in a smart  way trump gets reelected period  this gets me to the distraction attempts  that have been very successful by the  right  when donald trump generates a firestorm  around whether this or that person is  racist  or whether a comment was racist or  whatever  these are important issues but they are  not  issues that are going to get swing state  voters  to abandon donald trump or motivate  anyone to get out and vote  if they see an endless focus and debate  over  whether this or that comment was racist  as an example  now i know that there are people on the  left who won't like this but  it's just the reality and then  unfortunately i spoke a year ago about  my desire for this not to happen  democrats and their supporters are  starting to slam each other  in a way that could be self-destructive  and just help donald trump  we are seeing i'm going in no particular  order here  we're seeing a rise of a no biden no way  contingent  and i agree that joe biden is not a  progressive but i also remember  all those people who said in 2016 who  cares hillary would be the same as trump  and of course they couldn't have been  more wrong look at the supreme court  look at the 25 percent of judges that  donald trump  has appointed and we're reminded every  day  that and the geopolitical belligerence  and now  trying to collude with enforcing  collusion with another country ukraine  we'll talk about that later  could not have been more different from  hillary clinton so that's a concern  then we have the growing group of bernie  supporters  focusing their ire on elizabeth warren  even mass unsubscribing from my youtube  channel last week when i pointed out hey  in 60 of recent polls warren has  surpassed bernie into second place  this group claiming warren is a tool of  the establishment disguised to appear  progressive and i'm  a shill merely for mentioning poll  results bernie and warren are not the  same  that's clear but that is another  contingent  that is potentially self-destructive and  it's getting to the point where it could  be damaging in the general election  the tulsi people i've already talked  about andrew yang's followers who  although relatively small mathematically  are getting extremely angry with just  like everything every anything that  happens they're absolutely furious about  then you've got biden supporters who are  falling  for the often repeated right-wing  talking points about  bernie and warren are extreme  they are radical they're too far left  they're even talking about the term  socialism that's the  contingent of biden supporters that's  terrible  this is the type of stuff that will  propel donald trump to reelection  because it feeds narratives that are not  useful to the left so i'm not saying  this because i'm looking to attack  a particular candidate or the supporters  of a particular candidate this isn't  even about  particular candidates this is merely  pragmatism we saw what happened in 2016  and unless we prevent these things i'm  mentioning from getting completely out  of control  it's going to happen again and we'll  have four more years of trump now there  are people in the audience  who would rather have four more years of  trump  than whoever you don't like from the  democratic primary right there are  people who would say  burn it all down let trump do whatever  he wants to do  because it's better than having whoever  it is that's running in the democratic  primary  i just disagree with that as a strategy  i think that the more we look at history  the more we realize  that what has worked historically is not  uh foregoing small changes we could  make right now with the idea of  eventually burning it all down and  building it back up in a perfect image  of what is perfectly aligned  with our political ideology that's not  the way it's worked  in the last however many however however  many years you consider to be modern  politics  that's simply not a strategy that's  worked so i'm open to having my mind  changed if you think you can convince me  that the let trump have another four  years burn it all down and then we'll be  in a much better position for 2024  mentality if you want to try to convince  me of that  i'm more than open to hearing from you  but it's not something that i see backed  by history  it's not something i see backed by logic  and it's not something that seems like  the right approach  let me know what you think i'm open to  having my mind changed about  all of this but i am increasingly  concerned because i don't want to see  another four years of donald trump yeah  i know it'd be great for the show  but i care about the country even more  than that uh  and i want to hear from you if you  disagree with me i'm on twitter  deepakman  the show is on twitter at  davidpakmanshow

